\par \pard \qc \page {\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Quadrature_Mixers}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Quadrature Mixers}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Quadrature Mixers}} {\b\fs44 
QUADRATURE MIXERS
\par }\pard {\f5 \tab 
Two high level integrated circuit mixers are used to give good Intermodulation performance especially for the second order products.   The mixers have also been chosen for their very low local oscillator to input leakage.  Gain control of the mixers,  +1
0dB    0dB and   -10 dB, is achieved by switching their output impedance.  Active low pass filters are used to provide 20 dB of gain to both of the base band quadrature outputs.  The quadrature outputs are connected to a stereo  jack
 for connection to the dsp card. In the transmit mode the quadrature base band outputs from the sound card are applied to the mixer inputs. The output  from the mixer is at the -10dBm to -20dBm level.  There is no harmonic filtering on this output as its 
only use is as an exciter for further filtered amplification, or for signal generator applications where the harmonics are accepted. 
